WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.790
Here's a quartic: two x to the
four, minus fourteen x cubed,

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.980
plus eighteen x squared, plus fourteen x,

3
00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.540
minus twenty, equals zero.

4
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:16.230
On a GDC, its graph crosses the
x axis four times: four roots.

5
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.190
And someone claims they add up to
seven, without solving anything.

6
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.540
How could you know that?

7
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.020
Add up the coefficients?

8
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.950
Or must you solve it first?

9
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.350
In this mission, you'll
see that each root,

10
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.770
alpha, gives a factor, x minus alpha.

11
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.670
Roots are where the
graph meets the x axis.

12
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.300
So you can build a polynomial backwards:
its leading coefficient times the product

13
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.520
of its factors.

14
00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.030
Then expand.

15
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:45.790
Your mission: work out how to add the
four roots without finding any of them.
